{"key": "337fdc9b296ccc82", "role": "operator", "t": 1790993175.191, "seconds": 5.701, "output": "To solve this task, we need to compare the two input strings and determine if they represent the same function. We can use a simple string comparison after normalizing the strings to remove any differences in case.\n\n1. Convert both strings to lower case to make the comparison case-insensitive.\n2. Remove any leading or trailing whitespace from both strings.\n3. Compare the normalized strings.\n\nIf the normalized strings are equal or one is a subset of the other (ignoring the word \"department\"), we can consider them as having the same function.\n\nLet's implement this logic:\n\n```python\ndef compare_functions(str1, str2):\n    # Normalize the strings\n    str1 = str1.lower().strip()\n    str2 = str2.lower().strip()\n    \n    # Remove \"department\" from str2 if present\n    if \"department\" in str2:\n        str2 = str2.replace(\"department\", \"\").strip()\n    \n    # Compare the strings\n    if str1 in str2 or str2 in str1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        return 0\n\n# Test the function\nprint(compare_functions('NATURAL RESOURCES', 'Natural Resources Department'))\n```\n\n0"}
